WEBVTT

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:08.465
Uh...
[nervous chuckle]

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.804
Here, here.

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:15.722
- What are you doing?
- I'm giving it all back.

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:17.432
Huh?

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:20.477
[Wolf] Excuse me.

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:25.023
What happened back there?

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:27.359
- I couldn't do it.
- What do you mean you couldn't do it?

00:00:27.443 --> 00:00:28.735
- [Wolf] I just...
- No!

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.654
I do not run.

00:00:30.738 --> 00:00:33.073
That is not how I roll.

00:00:33.157 --> 00:00:34.866
Piranha, don't do anything crazy.

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:36.493
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.621
"Crazy" is what I bring
to the party, chico.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.128
[Shark groans]

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.132
<i>You're makin' a mistake. We didn't do it.</i>

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.593
<i>I know we always say that,</i>
<i>but this time it's actually true.</i>

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:54.595
<i>La, la, la, la, la. Can't hear you.</i>

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:56.972
<i>- Guilty, guilty, guilty!</i>
<i>- Talk to Marmalade.</i>

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.849
<i>We're really good now.</i>
<i>He'll tell you.</i>

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:00.100
<i>Professor...</i>

00:01:00.184 --> 00:01:02.477
<i>Tonight's headline: Change is Impossible.</i>

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.563
You should always judge a book
by its cover,

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:07.024
and all stereotypes
have been affirmed.

00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:09.943
Stop, for goodness' sake!
Let me speak to them.

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:12.321
I'm sure there's been
some misunderstanding.

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:14.031
[door opens]

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:15.657
[sighs] Professor Marmalade.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.202
You've got five minutes.
No deals this time.

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:22.247
You have to help us. Tell them.
Tell them we didn't do it.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:25.208
There, there. Of course you didn't do it.
How could you?

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:28.795
After all, you're such a good boy.

00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:32.799
You're such a good boy.

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:37.512
That shiver up my spine.
The wag in my tiny tail.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.430
Arrest them!

00:01:38.514 --> 00:01:40.515
What if we tried
a little experiment, Diane?

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.060
As you know,
my Gala for Goodness...

00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:45.312
[Tiffany Fluffit]
<i>Where the legendary Love Crater Meteorite</i>

00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:48.106
<i>will be on display</i>
<i>for the first time ever.</i>

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:51.109
All eyes will be on you tonight, not me.

00:01:52.236 --> 00:01:53.278
<i>You're such a...</i>

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:55.614
[low voice] Goodboy.

00:01:56.532 --> 00:01:58.241
You.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:00.160
It was all you.

00:02:00.244 --> 00:02:01.578
What are you talkin' about, Wolf?

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:03.830
The old lady, the Golden Dolphin,
good training...

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.207
It was all to get us here

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.626
so he could steal the meteorite
and let us take the fall.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.378
Whoa, what old lady?

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.214
And why would a guinea pig
want a meteorite anyway?

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.549
[Marmalade cackling]

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.386
Uh, guys? He's creepin' me out.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.553
Wait, what?

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.639
What's goin' on?
Someone turn me around.

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:24.393
Well, well. So, you finally get it.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.644
[all] What?

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:27.562
You stole the meteorite?

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.690
It's not just a meteorite.

00:02:29.774 --> 00:02:31.149
I told you guys it's a butt.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.484
It's not a butt!

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:36.655
[exhales]
It's the ultimate power source.

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.490
You see, when it struck,

00:02:38.574 --> 00:02:41.326
<i>scientists found that it emitted</i>
<i>an electromagnetic frequency</i>

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.495
<i>unlike anything else on earth.</i>

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:45.789
I'm going to harness its power to pull off

00:02:45.873 --> 00:02:48.417
the greatest heist
the world has ever seen.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.294
You should've eaten him
when you had the chance.

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:53.004
- Yep.
- But why us?

00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:55.549
Because you're the perfect patsies.

00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:58.885
Come on, when people look up "bad"
in the dictionary,

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.555
do they see a sweet, adorable guinea pig?

00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:03.473
No. They see you.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.600
And they always will.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.102
Okay. Fine.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.687
But you set us up.

00:03:08.771 --> 00:03:10.272
Oh, pish-pish.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.734
Let's be honest. Evolution set you up.

00:03:13.818 --> 00:03:15.902
But Wolfie here really clinched it.

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:18.488
You fell for every one of my traps,

00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:21.658
starting with saving
a helpless little old lady.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.120
Wolf. What's he talkin' about?

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:29.291
[Marmalade] Whoops.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.334
Did I say too much?

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.755
Anyhoo, looks like yet again

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:38.425
the big, bad wolf got outsmarted
by a little piggy.

00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:41.386
[growls] You little pouchy-cheeked rat!

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:43.054
I'll kill you, you hear me?

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:44.973
- [Marmalade] Help! Help!
- You're dead! You're dead...

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.434
Help!
The big, bad wolf is attacking me.

00:03:47.518 --> 00:03:49.853
Now you are done forever, Wolf!

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.779
[sirens wailing]

00:03:58.863 --> 00:03:59.905
[Marmalade shuddering]

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:02.866
Professor, Professor,
any thoughts on how the Bad Guys

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.285
managed to steal the meteorite
in plain sight?

00:04:05.369 --> 00:04:06.870
Well, off the top of my head,

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:08.580
perhaps they accessed
the site previously

00:04:08.664 --> 00:04:11.333
and set up an intricate system
of tunnels and trapdoors

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.503
that could be remotely triggered to suck
the meteorite down into a holding area.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.129
- But how should I know?
- [Tiffany Fluffit] Totally.

00:04:16.214 --> 00:04:19.216
[Marmalade] I mean,
they're the deranged masterminds. Not me.

00:04:41.322 --> 00:04:42.697
<i>[Wolf] I'm giving it all back.</i>

